    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can create personalized practice problems, explain concepts in simple language, and offer instant feedback. For example, they could adapt to a student’s mistakes in real time, helping them learn at their own pace. This makes math more accessible and engaging, especially for those who struggle with traditional methods."
